examples.question_text:
From the graph, state the intercepts, axis of symmetry, vertex and minimum value of $y$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black,<->},xmin=-3.5,xmax=5.5,ymin=-5,ymax=6,xtick={-3,-2,...,5},ytick={-4,-3,...,5},grid=major,grid style={draw=gray!40},ticklabel style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$},scaled ticks=false]
\addplot[color=curveblue,thick,<->,domain=-2.1:4.1,samples=100] {0.5*(x+2)*(x-4)};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The curve crosses the horizontal axis at $(-2,0)$ and $(4,0)$, and the vertical axis at $(0,-4)$.

Find the midpoint of the two $x$-intercepts:
$\begin{align*}x&=\frac{-2+4}{2}\\x&=1\end{align*}$

The axis of symmetry is $x=1$. Read the turning point on this line: the vertex is $(1,-4.5)$.

The parabola opens upwards, so the vertex is a minimum. The minimum value is $y=-4.5$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black,<->},xmin=-3.5,xmax=5.5,ymin=-5.5,ymax=6,xtick={-2,1,4},ytick={2,4},ticklabel style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},every axis plot/.append style={line width=0.8pt},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$},scaled ticks=false]
\addplot[color=curveblue,thick,<->,domain=-2.1:4.1,samples=100] {0.5*(x+2)*(x-4)};
\draw[black,dashed] (axis cs:1,-5) -- (axis cs:1,5);
\addplot[black,only marks,mark=*] coordinates {(-2,0) (4,0) (0,-4) (1,-4.5)};
\node[anchor=south east,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] at (axis cs:-2,0) {$(-2,0)$};
\node[anchor=south west,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] at (axis cs:4,0) {$(4,0)$};
\node[anchor=east,xshift=-4mm,yshift=3mm,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] at (axis cs:0,-4) {$(0,-4)$};
\node[anchor=north west,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] at (axis cs:1,-4.5) {$(1,-4.5)$};
\node[anchor=west,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] at (axis cs:1,4.5) {$x=1$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
From the graph, state how many $x$-intercepts there are and give their coordinates. Also state the $y$-intercept, vertex, axis of symmetry and maximum value of $y$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black,<->},xmin=-3.5,xmax=2.5,ymin=-5,ymax=2,xtick={-3,-2,...,2},ytick={-4,-3,...,1},grid=major,grid style={draw=gray!40},ticklabel style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$},scaled ticks=false]
\addplot[color=curveblue,thick,<->,domain=-3.1:1.1,samples=100] {-(x+1)*(x+1)};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The curve touches the horizontal axis at $(-1,0)$, so there is one $x$-intercept. It crosses the vertical axis at $(0,-1)$.

The turning point is also $(-1,0)$. The vertical line through it is the axis of symmetry, $x=-1$.

The parabola opens downwards, so the vertex is a maximum. The maximum value is $y=0$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black,<->},xmin=-3.5,xmax=2.5,ymin=-5,ymax=2,xtick={-3,-2,...,2},ytick={-4,-3,...,1},ticklabel style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$},scaled ticks=false]
\addplot[color=curveblue,thick,<->,domain=-3.1:1.1,samples=100] {-(x+1)*(x+1)};
\draw[black,dashed] (axis cs:-1,-4.5) -- (axis cs:-1,1.5);
\addplot[black,only marks,mark=*] coordinates {(-1,0) (0,-1)};
\node[anchor=south east,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] at (axis cs:-1,0) {$(-1,0)$};
\node[anchor=north west,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] at (axis cs:0,-1) {$(0,-1)$};
\draw[black] (axis cs:-1,1.4) -- (axis cs:-1.7,1.4);
\node[anchor=east,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] at (axis cs:-1.7,1.4) {$x=-1$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
From the graph, state the vertex, axis of symmetry, $y$-intercept and minimum value of $y$. Explain how many $x$-intercepts the parabola has.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black,<->},xmin=-4.5,xmax=2.5,ymin=-1,ymax=8,xtick={-4,-3,...,2},ytick={0,1,...,7},grid=major,grid style={draw=gray!40},ticklabel style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$},scaled ticks=false]
\addplot[color=curveblue,thick,<->,domain=-3.5:1.5,samples=100] {(x+1)*(x+1)+1};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Read the turning point: the vertex is $(-1,1)$. The axis of symmetry is the vertical line $x=-1$.

The curve crosses the vertical axis at $(0,2)$.

The parabola opens upwards, so the vertex is a minimum and the minimum value is $y=1$. The whole curve lies above the horizontal axis, so there are no $x$-intercepts.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black,<->},xmin=-4.5,xmax=2.5,ymin=-1,ymax=8,xtick={-4,-3,...,2},ytick={0,1,...,7},ticklabel style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$},scaled ticks=false]
\addplot[color=curveblue,thick,<->,domain=-3.5:1.5,samples=100] {(x+1)*(x+1)+1};
\draw[black,dashed] (axis cs:-1,0) -- (axis cs:-1,7);
\addplot[black,only marks,mark=*] coordinates {(-1,1) (0,2)};
\node[anchor=north east,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] at (axis cs:-1,1) {$(-1,1)$};
\node[anchor=south west,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] at (axis cs:0,2) {$(0,2)$};
\node[anchor=west,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] at (axis cs:-1,6.5) {$x=-1$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
